 # 16. Extension Constraints
 
 Classification extensions shall satisfy the following constraints.
 
+---
+
 ## 16.1. E-001 — No Semantic Redefinition
 
-Existing Classification semantics shall not be modified by an extension.
-
-A new element shall not redefine an existing element.
+Ordinary additions shall preserve existing applicable meaning. Necessary explicitly assessed semantic or mandate revision follows§79 rather than an absolute freeze.
+
+A new element shall not silently redefine an existing element;actual explicit necessary revision must identify and revise prior mandates under responsible authority.
+
+**Current governing scope.** E-001 retains its source-specific constraint identity/title and no-silent-change obligation. The explicit necessary-revision route does not make old and new contradictory mandates concurrently canonical. Original wording remains full input evidence,not a second operative absolute freeze.
 
 ---
 
